{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:c22bc8f182c8a1b0","name":"Ion Pulse Cannon","source":{"id":"source:reference-c22bc8f182c8a1b0","title":"Ion Pulse Cannon","revision":19944,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:54:18Z","sha256":"55504021094fcc336ab4345b79ea736e5e634c5e73ad7273125fa7c8161c5185","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19944","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Ion%20Pulse%20Cannon&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-c22bc8f182c8a1b0","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 9d10x10 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion"},")\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Ion Pulse Cannon is found on ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Subjugator"]},"-Class Heavy Cruisers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Subjugator-Class_Heavy_Cruisers"}," and is used to disable enemy ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," before they have a chance to fire back. No other class of ship carries the weapon due to its unique power generation needs.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Ion Pulse Cannons are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Area Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Area_Attack"}," weapons, even at ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"},". A single Ion Pulse Cannon targets all ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," within 5 squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"},") of the ship carrying the weapon; the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," makes an attack roll against each ship within that area. On a hit; the target takes normal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion"}," damage and moves -2 steps on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},". On a miss, the target takes half damage and moves -1 step on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Unlike most other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"},", Ion Pulse Cannons have a significant build-up and cooldown time. The weapon can be fired as normal as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},". However, after firing the Ion Pulse Cannon, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," must spend three consecutive ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Actions"}," clearing the weapon of ionized particles before it can be fired again. If the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," takes damage that equals or exceeds its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"}," at any time during this recharge period, the Ion Pulse Cannon automatically overloads and is destroyed.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
